{title: There’s a Song in the Air}
{artist: Josiah G. Holland / Karl P. Harrington}
{genre: Christmas}
{style: Carol}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Sing to the Lord (Kansas City, Missouri: Lillenas Publishing Company, 1993), # 196)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]There’s a song in the [D7]air!
[D7]There’s a [G]star in the [D7]sky!
[D7]There’s a [G]mother’s deep [D]prayer
[A7]And a baby’s low [D7]cry!
[D7]And the [Em]star [G]rains its fire
[G]While the [D7]beautiful sing,
[D7]For the [G7]manger of [Am]Beth[C]lehem
[Bm]Cra[D7]dles a [G]king!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]There’s a tumult of [D7]joy
[D7]O’er the [G]wonderful [D7]birth,
[D7]For the [G]virgin’s sweet [D]boy
[A7]Is the Lord of the [D7]earth.
[D7]Ay! the [Em]star [G]rains its fire
[G]While the [D7]beautiful sing,
[D7]For the [G7]manger of [Am]Beth[C]lehem
[Bm]Cra[D7]dles a [G]king!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]In the light of that [D7]star
[D7]Lie the [G]ages im[D7]pearled;
[D7]And that [G]song from a[D]far
[A7]Has swept over the [D7]world.
[D7]Every [Em]hearth [G]is aflame,
[G]And the [D7]beautiful sing
[D7]In the [G7]homes of the [Am]na[C]tions
[C]That [Bm]Je[D7]sus is [G]king!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]We rejoice in the [D7]light,
[D7]And we [G]echo the [D7]song
[D7]That comes [G]down through the [D]night
[A7]From the heavenly [D7]throng.
[D7]Ay! we [Em]shout [G]to the lovely
[G]E[D7]vangel they bring,
[D7]And we [G7]greet in His [Am]cra[C]dle
[C]Our [Bm]Sav[D7]ior and [G]king!
{end_of_verse}
